GFX1013 (AMD BC-250): expose the dedicated compute (ACE) queue in RADV and route its dispatches through the
existing async compute threadgroup workaround of Iceland and Tonga (thread-dimension dispatch mode). Without that
workaround, threadgroup-dimension dispatches on the ACE queue mis-execute and RADV's own copy shaders drop rows.

From DryhoppedIPA/bc250-gfx1013-fix (MIT) patch 0001, as trimmed for Bazzite's kernel by
tri3gubki-ops/bc250-async-compute-bazzite (MIT): the GFX10.1 version fix-up of the original is upstream since
Mesa 26.2.1. The file it changes is Mesa's, MIT (Copyright © 2017 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.).

--- a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
@@ -483,11 +483,9 @@
        */
       info->ip[ip_type].num_queues = 1;
    } else if (ip_info->available_rings) {
-      /* GFX1013 is known to have broken compute queue */
-      if (ip_type == AMD_IP_COMPUTE && device_info->family == FAMILY_NV &&
-          ASICREV_IS(device_info->external_rev, GFX1013))
-         return false;
-
+      /* GFX1013 (BC-250): the dedicated compute queue is exposed. It works once its dispatches take the
+       * async compute threadgroup workaround below (has_async_compute_threadgroup_bug).
+       */
       info->ip[ip_type].num_queues = util_bitcount(ip_info->available_rings);
    }
 
@@ -1020,7 +1018,8 @@
     * dimension mode.
     */
    info->has_async_compute_threadgroup_bug = info->family == CHIP_ICELAND ||
-                                             info->family == CHIP_TONGA;
+                                             info->family == CHIP_TONGA ||
+                                             info->family == CHIP_GFX1013;
 
